  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep veggies: Thinly slice half the onion, then finely chop the remaining onion. Coarsely chop the cashews. Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove. Wipe the mushrooms clean, then quarter. Drain and rinse the chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146886/photos/large/prep_veggies-0c3972b93e3a058c8937e63bfb29681a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Caramelise onion: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a large frypan over medium-low heat (see Make it faster). Cook the onion slices, stirring occasionally, for 6-8 mins until caramelised. Remove with tongs and drain on paper towel.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146887/photos/large/caramelise_onion-b16fc8b08646983de09546bcbde165b2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook mushrooms and spices: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in the same pan over high heat. Cook the mushrooms, stirring occasionally, for 5 mins or until softened. Add the chopped onion, garlic, half the cashews and 2 tsp garam masala and cook, stirring occasionally, for a further 3 mins or until soft.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146888/photos/large/cook_mushrooms_and_spices-76bab5a2fe741a455b48edf5f6f4be49.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add tomatoes and simmer: Add the chickpeas, tomatoes, 125ml (½ cup) water and ½ tsp honey to the mushroom mixture and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to low and cook for 5 mins for the flavours to develop.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146889/photos/large/add_tomatoes_and_simmer-783e23dda6122a147032f97204df5889.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the peas and cook for a further 3 mins or until warmed through. Taste, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the stew among bowls, scatter over the caramelised onion and remaining cashews and enjoy.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146890/photos/large/serve_up-2539ed4870e9f3d4af6ddb07b2dc2699.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it faster: Speed things up by cooking the onion in a separate frypan while you get the mushrooms going.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/146891/photos/large/make_it_yours-5cf90205605dff943b1a4abc74a6bf96.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
